DTEND:20261120T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: HIIG Impact AI Fellowship 2027 (EUR 5\,000\, 10
  weeks\, Berlin and remote)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 20 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nHIIG's Impact AI Fellowship
  invites people interested in measuring the effects of AI on society and t
 he environment to assess an existing\, operational AI application and take
  lead authorship of a published case report. Applicants do not need their 
 own case\; HIIG helps match fellows with cases\, and proposed cases must b
 e deployed applications rather than prototypes or research ideas.\n\nOrgan
 isation: Alexander von Humboldt Institute for Internet and Society (HIIG)\
 nLocation: Berlin\, Germany (two mandatory in-person weeks\; other weeks c
 an be remote). No nationality restriction stated.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 fixed
  stipend per fellow for the ten weeks (inclusive of any tax or social secu
 rity in the fellow's home country)\, with case-by-case partial support for
  in-person costs. No application fee mentioned.\nDuration: 10 weeks\, 16 A
 ugust to 22 October 2027\, with in-person weeks in Berlin on 16-20 August 
 and 4-8 October 2027 and a mandatory online preparatory session on 11 May 
 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.hiig.de/en/impact-ai-call-for-fellows/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.hiig.de/en/impact-ai-call-for-fellows/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany (two mandatory in-person weeks\; other weeks can 
 be remote). No nationality restriction stated.
END:VEVENT
