SUMMARY:Deadline: SVDJ Incubator 2027: Jongeren en Journalistiek (nine-mont
 h journalism innovation programme\; EUR 20\,000 to 40\,000 participation s
 ubsidy)
DESCRIPTION:The SVDJ Incubator is the Dutch Journalism Fund's innovation pr
 ogramme in which multidisciplinary teams spend nine months researching\, e
 xperimenting and testing around one sector-wide question\; all outcomes ar
 e published open source. The 2027 theme is Jongeren en Journalistiek: how 
 journalism can build durable strategies to strengthen the information posi
 tion of young people aged 16 to 24.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds voo
 r de Journalistiek (SVDJ)\nLocation: Utrecht\, Netherlands (free office sp
 ace near Utrecht Centraal\; mandatory in-person kick-off\, start weekend a
 nd meetings). Programme and call are in Dutch.\nAward: Participation subsi
 dy for the whole programme: EUR 20\,000 at 0.4 fte (16 hours a week)\, EUR
  30\,000 at 0.6 fte (24 hours) or EUR 40\,000 at 0.8 fte (32 hours). Plus 
 a travel allowance of EUR 0 to 400 a month depending on distance to Utrech
 t (up to EUR 3\,600 in total)\; the page lists the application amount as E
 UR 20\,000 to 43\,600. A further EUR 400\,000 pot is available to teams du
 ring the programme for short projects and experiments. If you are seconded
  by an employer\, the employer receives the subsidy.\nDuration: Nine month
 s\, 2 March to 30 November 2027\n\nMore: https://www.svdj.nl/regeling/svdj
 -incubator/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.svdj.nl/regeling/svdj-incubator/?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Utrecht\, Netherlands (free office space near Utrecht Centraal\; m
 andatory in-person kick-off\, start weekend and meetings). Programme and c
 all are in Dutch.
END:VEVENT
